# Project: TPE Short Links

## Goal
Build an internal URL shortener with:
- Create short link: {domain}/{CODE}, CODE is [A-Za-z0-9]+ (case-sensitive).
- Redirect endpoint: GET /{CODE} redirects to original_url when valid.
- Links are never reusable: once a CODE is used, it can never be used again, even after expiry.
- Users must select a tag and an expiry date (expiry can be permanent).
- Certain “special combinations” are blocked (reserved codes).

## Default technical choices (unless repo already dictates otherwise)
- Backend: FastAPI + Postgres + SQLAlchemy + Alembic
- Frontend: React + Vite + TypeScript + Mantine UI
- Prefer simple, explicit code over abstractions.

## Non-negotiable behavior rules
- Treat CODE as case-sensitive everywhere (routing, DB collation, comparisons).
- Never delete ShortLink rows. Use status flags (active/expired/disabled/blocked).
- Expiry semantics:
  - expires_at = NULL means permanent
  - expires_at <= now means expired
- Redirect behavior:
  - active: 302 redirect to original_url
  - expired: 410 Gone (or a dedicated expired page, but default 410)
  - blocked/disabled/not found: 404 Not Found
- Reserved codes:
  - Must be rejected on creation (generator must never output them)
  - Must not be routable for redirect even if present in DB.

## UX requirements
- Create page: URL input, Tag dropdown, Expiry (Permanent / Date), Note, Create button.
- Result panel: show short URL + copy button.
- Manage page: list/search/filter; allow disabling a link.
- No authentication requirements for now.

## Working style
- When implementing, always:
  1) Update DB/migrations first,
  2) Implement backend endpoints,
  3) Implement frontend UI consuming those endpoints,
  4) Add tests for edge cases and concurrency.
